```

Is code ko copy karke `.html` file ke taur par save karo aur browser mein run kar lo!

Samajh gaya bhai! Free public API nahi, balki jo tu upar **ChatGPT-Web2API** ya **Web2API (local server)** ki baat kar raha tha, uske local backend (`http://localhost:8080`) se connect karne wala all-in-one HTML client yeh raha:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Local Web2API Chat Hub</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4"></script>
</head>
<body class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 flex flex-col h-screen p-4 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
    <header class="flex justify-between items-center border-b border-slate-800 pb-4 mb-4">
        <h1 class="text-xl font-bold text-cyan-400">⚡ Local Web2API Hub</h1>
        <select id="apiProvider" class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 text-sm rounded px-2 py-1 text-slate-300">
            <option value="chatgpt">ChatGPT-Web2API (Local)</option>
            <option value="gemini">Gemini (Web2API)</option>
            <option value="perplexity">Perplexity (Web2API)</option>
        </select>
    </header>
    <div id="chatBox" class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto space-y-3 pr-2 mb-4 text-sm">
        <div class="bg-slate-900 p-3 rounded-lg max-w-[80%] text-slate-300">Bhai, apna local backend (port 8080) start karke message bhejo!</div>
    </div>
    <form id="chatForm" class="flex gap-2">
        <input type="text" id="userInput" placeholder="Ask your local model..." class="flex-1 bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded px-3 py-2 text-sm focus:outline-none focus:border-cyan-500" required>
        <button type="submit" class="bg-cyan-600 hover:bg-cyan-500 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded text-sm font-medium">Send</button>
    </form>
    <script>
        const chatBox = document.getElementById('chatBox'), chatForm = document.getElementById('chatForm'), userInput = document.getElementById('userInput');
        chatForm.onsubmit = async (e) => {
            e.preventDefault();
            const text = userInput.value, provider = document.getElementById('apiProvider').value;
            chatBox.innerHTML += `<div class="bg-cyan-950/50 p-3 rounded-lg max-w-[80%] ml-auto text-cyan-200">${text}</div>`;
            userInput.value = '';
            chatBox.scrollTop = chatBox.scrollHeight;
            try {
                const res = await fetch('http://localhost:8080/v1/chat/completions', {
                    method: 'POST',
                    headers: {'Content-Type': 'application/json'},
                    body: JSON.stringify({model: provider, messages: [{role: 'user', content: text}]})
                });
                const data = await res.json();
                const reply = data.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || "No response";
                chatBox.innerHTML += `<div class="bg-slate-900 p-3 rounded-lg max-w-[80%] text-slate-300">${reply}</div>`;
            } catch (err) {
                chatBox.innerHTML += `<div class="bg-red-950/50 p-3 rounded-lg max-w-[80%] text-red-300">Connection failed! Ensure local server is running on port 8080.</div>`;
            }
            chatBox.scrollTop = chatBox.scrollHeight;
        };
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

